export default JSON.parse("{\"schema\":\"ai-brain-source-note/1.0\",\"domain\":\"studio-tools\",\"capabilities\":[\"3d\",\"api\",\"auth\",\"class\",\"generator\",\"grid\",\"layer\",\"mobile\",\"quest\",\"search\"],\"provenance\":{\"sourceGroup\":\"player-reference-runtime-c\",\"sourceType\":\"provided-project-material\",\"archiveHash\":\"b25a1dee02bb3fec\"},\"title\":\"audit.md\",\"content\":\"# Final Repository Audit \u2014 v3.0.0\\n\\nGenerated: 2026-07-23\\n\\n## Failure found in v2\\n\\nThe previous package exposed a 3D-generation action but did not contain a complete creation pipeline:\\n\\n- `studio.html` was still described and guarded as import-only.\\n- The main AI screen had no functional request-to-creator bridge.\\n- Backend action `3d.generate` threw an error unless separate `THREED_API_URL` and `THREED_API_KEY` properties were configured.\\n- The generated result was not transferred into the Visual Studio.\\n- The directory form and bot controls competed for screen space, and the desktop composer could fall below the initial viewport.\\n\\n## Repairs implemented\\n\\n- Added `creator.html`, `assets/js/creator.js`, and `assets/css/creator.css` as an always-available browser procedural 3D generator.\\n- Added prompt classification so direct 3D creation requests typed into the bot automatically open the creator.\\n- Added transfer of attached reference images from IndexedDB into the creator.\\n- Added editable named components, material controls, part hierarchy, primitive insertion, duplication, deletion, wireframe/grid views, and Blender-style viewport/numeric transforms.\\n- Added GLB, OBJ, STL, and JSON-blueprint exports.\\n- Added transferable GLB `postMessage` bridge from creator to Visual Studio.\\n- Updated `studio.html` and `studio-app.js` to accept and edit generated GLB data.\\n- Replaced the backend hard failure with deterministic procedural blueprints and optional AI refinement/provider submission.\\n- Added `3d.plan` and revised `3d.generate` routes.\\n- Rebuilt the main workflow around Select \u2192 Ask \u2192 Create \u2192 Review \u2192 Save.\\n- Moved the full directory editor into a collapsible drawer and made directory cards/search the primary flow.\\n- Corrected desktop composer visibility and mobile min-width overflow.\\n- Added restricted-storage fallback behavior.\\n\\n## Validation performed\\n\\n- JavaScript syntax checks passed for all project-authored JavaScript files.\\n- Apps Script syntax parsing passed.\\n- A mocked Apps Script smoke test confirmed `3d.generate` returns a ready procedural blueprint without external provider credentials.\\n- The sample fountain request returned a container blueprint with five editable components and three materials.\\n- Main-interface browser rendering was checked at 1440\u00d71000 and 390\u00d7844; no page errors were reported in the isolated static test.\\n- Required DOM IDs and script references were checked.\\n- Three.js runtime bundles were checked for OrbitControls, TransformControls, GLTFExporter, OBJExporter, STLExporter, RoundedBoxGeometry, and CapsuleGeometry.\\n- Prohibited domain-specific terminology and disallowed legacy/archive paths are scanned by `scripts/verify.py`.\\n\\n## Deployment note\\n\\nA previously deployed Apps Script URL does not change merely because `backend/Code.gs` changed inside this ZIP. The user must replace the Apps Script project code and deploy a new version for cloud blueprint refinement. Local browser generation remains operational without that deployment.\\n\"}");
